Borrowed components (with modifications for spec-embedded-iot context):

  skills/spec-knowledge-archiver/scripts/wiki/helpers.py
    - Derived from mcp/tools/helpers.py
    - Modifications: removed deep_link (depends on hosted config);
      kept glob_match / resolve_path / parse_page_range (pure functions).

  skills/spec-knowledge-archiver/scripts/wiki/references.py
    - Derived from mcp/tools/references.py
    - Modifications: kept only parse_citation_filename and parse_wiki_links
      (pure functions); removed update_references / get_backlinks_summary
      (depended on VaultFS async storage layer).

  skills/spec-knowledge-archiver/scripts/wiki/frontmatter.py
    - Derived from mcp/tools/write.py (frontmatter-related functions)
    - Modifications: removed FastMCP / VaultFS dependencies;
      renamed private _parse_frontmatter etc. to public parse_frontmatter etc.

  skills/spec-knowledge-archiver/scripts/wiki/chunker.py
    - Derived from mcp/services/chunker.py
    - Modifications: removed store_chunks_pg / store_chunks_sqlite (DB persistence);
      kept chunk_text + Chunk dataclass + helpers (pure functions).
      Purpose changed: originally for vector indexing, now only used by lint
      (estimate document size, check oversized paragraphs).

  skills/spec-knowledge-archiver/scripts/wiki/guide.py
    - Inspired by mcp/tools/guide.py (GUIDE_TEXT pattern)
    - Modifications: heavily customized for embedded IoT context
      (5 knowledge types: bug-solutions / code-summary / requirement-solutions /
      official-docs / project-overview; platform isolation in raw/, global wiki/).

  skills/spec-knowledge-archiver/scripts/wiki/lint.py
    - Inspired by mcp/tools/lint.py (LintHandler pattern)
    - Modifications: removed MCP FastMCP registration; removed VaultFS dependency;
      replaced direct filesystem reads; trimmed checks to frontmatter / type /
      broken-link / orphan-entry (removed citation-graph checks since we use
      wikilinks not footnote citations, and removed stale_page which needed DB tracking).

